# Date display format

User-facing dates are **`22 Sep 2026`**: day with no leading zero, English 3-letter month (`Jan`–`Dec`), then year.

## Source of truth

- Display with `formatDisplayDate()` / `formatDisplayDateTime()` from `src/lib/format.ts`
- Date-time: `22 Sep 2026 4:10 PM`
- Persist and send ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (and ISO datetimes) in state, APIs, and `<input type="date">` values

## Do

```tsx
formatDisplayDate('2026-09-22') // 22 Sep 2026
<DateInput value={iso} onChange={setIso} className="input" />
```

## Don't

- Don't show `22/09/2026`, `2026-09-22`, or `22 Sept 2026` in the UI
- Don't call `toLocaleDateString()` or `Intl.DateTimeFormat` for dates
- Don't put a visible native date input; wrap pickers in `DateInput` so the overlay shows `22 Sep 2026`
- Don't invent a second formatter in a page or print template
